# Patch branches applied on top of `staging`, in order, to build `luma/staging`.
# One branch per line, then `#` and one sentence for the release notes of the fork build.
# patch/fork-tooling is applied after these by rebuild.sh; do not list it.
patch/slurp-collab-in-picture # A collab's joint post or a couple's date draws the partner into the picture at every level.
patch/slurp-appearance-clothes # Clothes are removed from Stage appearance too, so nude pictures no longer come out dressed.
patch/slurp-writer-outfit # A post whose writer names no saved look keeps the writer's own outfit.
patch/slurp-bare-outfit # An outfit of "completely naked" or "fully nude" counts as no outfit.
patch/slurp-locked-scene # About half of a Creator's own locked posts keep their scene, and the spicy kind no longer repeats back to back.
patch/slurp-opener-all-posts # The overused-opener check reads every recent post, locked ones included.
patch/slurp-unique-sequence # Every post generation draws on its own sequence, so two posts no longer get the same details.
patch/slurp-card-interests # A card's likes and hobbies reach every post, and section headings are no longer read as facts.
patch/slurp-quiet-days # Quiet days are one line in the recent-activity list, so real activity fills it.
patch/slurp-card-core # The card's core in every brief is about four times longer.
patch/slurp-character-ideas # Creators choose each automatic post's idea from their whole card, and a new setting sets the locked share.
